WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:07.019
Speaker 1: Marjorie Taylor Greene has appeared
on conspiracy theorist Alex Jones Infowars,

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:10.960
and she wants to make it known that she is
not crazy.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.160
She says it bothers her to be treated like
she's a crazy person.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.730
This is all starting to be beyond parody.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:20.680
Let's take a listen to Marjorie Taylor Greene.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.470
Speaker 6: And it just bothers me so much.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:28.270
They treat me as if I'm some kind of crazy
person, like I have three horns coming out

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.350
of my head.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:32.250
But what they don't understand is they're
the ones that are crazy, right?

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.860
Speaker 1: Everybody else is crazy.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.860
She's not.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.590
Everything she does is completely normal.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.400
And by the way, she says this with an info.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.680
More sign behind her, which is a choice to
do that.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.040
And she seems unable to realize that Alex
Jones is crazy.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.460
It's very similar to Mike Lindell.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:01.399
Claiming to have evidence that is going to
put 300 million people behind bars and then

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:06.550
saying everybody else is crazy because they
don't realize the evidence is so obvious at

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:12.630
a certain point, a non crazy person and I
get that these I'm not I'm not literally using

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.630
these terms.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.750
I'm not stigmatizing mental illness, but wacky.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:22.280
Maybe we use wacky or disconnected from reality
at a certain point, a person who's connected

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:28.090
to reality would realize when you say you
have evidence to imprison 300 million people

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:33.830
for their role in the 2020 election, you would
realize I'm the wacky one, right?

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.430
And it's the exact same thing, with Marjorie
Taylor Greene just completely disconnected

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:44.650
from her own reality that she's saying outrageous
things that no serious sane person could possibly

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.650
believe.

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:53.130
She also is continuing to say them, even as
she claims to be not crazy at an event in

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.689
Texas over the weekend, which we talked about
earlier earlier in the week.

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:00.960
She says, you know, AOC was a bartender, so
she's not smart.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.520
Speaker 6: OK.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.100
Where is that energy going to be created?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:09.170
Your solar and wind?

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:11.810
Don't you know?

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:20.870
Come on, AOC, so much smarter than all of
us, she was a bartender, right?

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:21.870
Right.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:28.260
You silly conservative Republicans, you probably
have small businesses and things like that.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.579
Shame on you, independent people that know
how to balance a checkbook right now.

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:39.870
Speaker 1: In all seriousness, people can
be smart coming from all walks of life.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:45.139
I know people who have every type of job you
could imagine, and they are smart people,

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:46.139
OK?

00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:51.159
But is Marjorie Taylor Greene's background
really anything to no one prove her intelligence

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:55.430
and number two to put her in a position to
make fun of other people's work backgrounds

00:02:55.430 --> 00:03:01.469
like Marjorie Taylor, Greene's dad gave her
and her husband his general contracting company.

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:02.469
Oh, OK, wow.

